WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.890
- Well, I heard that you
have a classic New York story

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.600
about a fake ID.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.100
This is sad, I think.
- Yeah, it's sad.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.780
- I think someone told me that.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.550
- Yeah, it's a sad story.
- Okay.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.450
- Okay, I was-

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.100
I mean, when I was a teenager,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.650
I grew up in Queens, so we
would take the subway into-

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.090
I liked to go to Times Square,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.820
which I feel horrible for my
parents now, looking back,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.770
because I would love to go to Times Square

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.670
all the time.
- Yeah, it's bright and shiny.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.900
- It's bright and shiny.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.630
So I once went with a
friend to Times Square

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.445
and I was walking around
and there was like-

00:00:26.445 --> 00:00:28.470
You know, you just hear like
distant voices in the crowd

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.930
that's like, "Tattoos,
piercings, fake IDs."

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.450
And I turned around and
I was like, "Fake IDs?"

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.680
So then the guy was like-

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.510
I was really young and stupid

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.980
and I was like, "Why not?"

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.660
So he was like, okay, but we're gonna-

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.630
So this is the plan, we
are gonna go to Roy Rogers,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.510
and like, I have to do some checks.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.620
So like, let's go to Roy Rogers.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.760
We went to Roy Rogers, which was,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.220
if you guys don't know, it
was an old chicken chain.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.060
- I did not.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.290
- You didn't know what Roy Rogers is?

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.660
- No, I think there's
like a coliseum in Texas.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.590
Maybe named that.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.423
Or Will Rogers.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.269
That's what it is.

00:00:57.269 --> 00:00:58.800
No, I don't know that one.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.390
- Roy Rogers, it's like a chicken-

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.530
It's like a chicken fast food place.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.090
So it was very public.
- I like chicken.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:03.923
Okay.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:06.870
So we went upstairs and
he pointed to a table.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:07.980
And he was like, you see that guy?

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.390
And there was a guy-

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.850
He was in a hat with what
looked like a trench coat.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.700
And he was like, that's my associate.

00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:15.487
And I was like, okay.

00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:17.804
Good to know that you
operated out Roy Rogers.

00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:22.110
He then was like, do you
have any bills on you?

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.460
Because I have to check that-

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.990
I have to make sure that
you're 15-years-old.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.850
You're not a CIA agent.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.860
So I need to get your bills off of you.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.280
So I had a $10 bill on me
and I gave him my $10 bill.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.510
And he was like, okay,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.640
I'm gonna go run this through the machine.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.620
Stay here, my associate's right there.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.847
And so he leaves and
like, 45 minutes goes by.

00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:45.270
I have a whole chicken meal, right?

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.590
And I keep eyeing his associate.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.520
He's like reading a newspaper,

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.370
doing very like, associate
things, you know?

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.800
And he didn't come back
for like, 45 minutes.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.410
So I get up and I kind of go
over to the his associate.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.786
And I'm like, excuse me sir, your partner-

00:01:57.786 --> 00:01:59.190
I just wanna make sure he's okay

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.380
that he didn't hit any road bumps.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.820
And he was like, what
are you talking about?

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.620
So he didn't even know that guy.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.360
He just made off with $10.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.120
- I love how sweet you
were at a young age,

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.680
I think 'cause I'm the youngest child,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.840
so much crap was pulled on me

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.290
that I would've been like BS.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.290
Like, you have such a
different childhood than me

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.060
that you believed in the good of people.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:21.893
- Yeah, I was like,

00:02:21.893 --> 00:02:23.820
"Yes, I of course I want
you to have this $10 bill

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.020
to check if I'm a CIA agent."

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.280
- Yes, I love that!

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.420
That's so horrible.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.560
But you got a chicken meal

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.803
and you got to meet a
nice man in a trench coat.

